.TH pwd "" "Command"
.SH NAME
pwd \- print current working directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpwd\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
pwd -- print current working directory
Usage:	pwd
.HE
.B pwd
prints the pathname of the current working directory.
It takes no arguments or options.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B sh
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B pwd
complains and exits with nonzero status if it cannot determine the
name of the current directory.
